BEHAVIOR array-get

DESCRIPTION
  Returns the element at index (0-based) of an int array. The caller is
  responsible for index < len (use array-len); out-of-range reads whatever the
  buffer holds at that slot.

CONTRACT
  INPUT arr bytes 65536
  INPUT index int 8
  OUTPUT value int 8
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 8c0f76d8

IMPLEMENTATION
  iv = LOAD index 8
  e = IMUL iv 8 8
  off = IADD e 16 8
  v = LOAD arr 8 off
  STORE value v 8
END
